 and\ncapacity-driven. If I used Engine 1 only, the DCF would understate value at the\ntrough (the classic cyclical trap); if I used Engine 4 (option-led), it would\noverstate permanence. Engine 2 is appropriate.\n\nStep 3-1. Cycle Position\nTrough: 2023-2025 (post-2022 peak). Recovery: Q2 2026 confirms inflection\n(volume +10% intermodal, revenue +19.4%, NI +40.7%).\nCycle stage: EARLY-MID RECOVERY (12-18 months in; 2026-27 likely strong;\n2028-29 risks maturity).\n\nStep 3-2. Normalized Earnings Power\n- Through-cycle revenue (2018-2025 avg): $11.66B [Arithmetic].\n- Forward mid-cycle revenue (2027 consensus +9% on 2026): \u2248 $14.15B [Estimate].\n- Normalized operating margin: 12-yr median 8.3%; recovery-high ~9.0-9.5%;\n  mid-cycle assumption: 8.5-9.0%. Use 8.8% for 2027 [Estimate/Assumption].\n- Normalized OI (2027): $14.15B \u00d7 8.8% = $1.245B [Estimate]\n- Less net interest: ~$55M [Estimate]\n- Pre-tax: $1.190B | Tax 24% [Assumption] | Net income: $905M\n- Shares: 94.0M (current) \u2014 2027 diluted count; shares still being bought back\n- Mid-cycle EPS: \u2248 $9.60 [Estimate]\n- Through-cycle (2018-25 average NI $662M / ~105M avg shares) EPS: $6.30 \u2014 this\n  is the floor reference.\n\nStep 3-3. Engine 2 Multiples\nFair multiple for fortress-moat cyclical at mid-cycle: 18-22x (leadership premium,\nROIC 12%, net debt 1.7B).\nFair value base: $9.60 \u00d7 20.5x = $197 \u2248 $200 [Estimate]\nBear multiple 15x trough-normalized $6.50 = $98; Bull 24x peak-normalized\n$11.50 = $276.\n\nStep 3-4. DCF Cross-Check (Engine 1 discipline \u2014 requires explicit forecast)\n\nExplicit forecast (Base):\n| Year | Revenue | Op Margin | OI | Tax | NOPAT | +D&A | \u2212Capex | \u2212\u0394WC | FCF |\n|------|---------|-----------|------|------|-------|------|--------|------|--------|\n| 2026E| 13.10   | 8.0%     | 1.048| 24%  | 0.797 | 0.740| 0.700  | 0.130| 0.707  |\n| 2027E| 14.15   | 8.8%     | 1.245| 24%  | 0.946 | 0.750| 0.800  | 0.120| 0.776  |\n| 2028E| 14.86   | 9.2%     | 1.367| 24%  | 1.039 | 0.760| 0.850  | 0.080| 0.869  |\n| 2029E| 15.38   | 9.3%     | 1.430| 24%  | 1.087 | 0.770| 0.850  | 0.050| 0.957  |\n| 2030E| 15.84   | 9.3%     | 1.473| 24%  | 1.120 | 0.780| 0.850  | 0.030| 1.020  |\n\nDriver sources:\n- Revenue 2026: +9% consensus [Estimate] and H1 run-rate ($6.55B) [Estimate];\n  Q2 annualized $13.98B implies upside risk to my 13.10.\n- Revenue 2027-2030: my assumption of decelerating freight recovery + structural\n  intermodal growth, ending at 3% \u2248 nominal GDP. [Assumption]\n- Operating margins: recovery path to 9.3% (below 2021-22 boom peak of ~9.8%\n  implied by OI 1.33/14.81 in 2022). [Assumption]\n- D&A: from FY2025 $715M growing ~1.5% with fleet. [Assumption]\n- Capex: 2026 net guide $600-800M [Actual \u2014 management]; 2027+ my assumption of\n  maintenance + modest growth, $800-850M. [Assumption]\n- \u0394WC: normalization after the 2023-25 cash releases. [Assumption]\n- Tax: 24% flat, my assumption (federal+state). [Assumption]\n\nDiscount rate derivation:\n- Risk-free: 4.71% [Actual \u2014 10Y, Aug 2026]\n- ERP: 4.7% [Assumption \u2014 long-run average]\n- Beta: 1.297 [Aggregator]\n- Cost of equity: 4.71% + 1.297 \u00d7 4.7% = 10.8% [Arithmetic]\n- Pre-tax cost of debt: 5.2% [Assumption \u2014 investment-grade logistics credit]\n- Weights: equity $25.87B / (equity + debt $1.70B) = 93.8%; debt 6.2%\n- WACC = 0.938 \u00d7 10.8% + 0.062 \u00d7 5.2% \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.24) = 10.34% \u2248 10.25% [Assumption]\n\nDCF result:\nPV explicit FCFs @10.25%: 641+638+648+648+626 = $3,201M\nTerminal growth: 2.5% \u2264 nominal GDP [Assumption]\nTerminal value = 1,020 \u00d7 1.025 / (0.1025 \u2212 0.025) = $13,490M\nPV of TV = $8,276M\nEV = $11,477M\nLess net debt $1,704M \u2192 Equity value = $9,773M\nPer share = $104 [Estimate]\n\nSENSITIVITY of DCF:\n- WACC 9.5% / g 2.5%: $126\n- WACC 10.25% / g 2.5%: $104\n- WACC 9.5% / g 3.0%: $142\nThe DCF yields $104-142/share \u2014 this is the classic cyclical DCF understatement\n(treating mid-cycle recovery cash flows as a perpetuity). I note it, weight it 30%,\nand weight the cycle-adjusted multiple more heavily (70%), because the cyclical\nengine is the correct primary. Blended IV \u2248 0.70\u00d7$200 + 0.30\u00d7$125 = $178.\n\nStep 3-5. Reverse DCF (what the market implies)\nTo justify $275.45: Shares 93.9M \u2192 equity $25.87B \u2192 EV \u2248 $27.57B.\nSubtract the PV of explicit FCFs (~$3.2B) \u2192 PV of terminal value must be $24.4B\n\u2192 terminal FCF must be $1.61B at 10.25%/2.5%, or $1.94B at WACC 9.5%/g 2.5%.\nA terminal FCF of $1.6-1.9B requires NOPAT of $1.7-2.0B at 2030 with ~$800M\ncapex \u2014 i.e., operating income of $2.2-2.6B on ~$18-20B revenue at ~11-13% margin.\nThat is ABOVE the 2022 boom (OI $1.33B on $14.8B revenue = 9.0%). Verdict: the\nmarket is pricing a structural re-rating BEYOND the prior peak. FEASIBLE only if\nintermodal conversion accelerates dramatically; I assign ~25-30% probability.\n\n3-X. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3 variables)\n1. 2027-28 operating margin (8.5-10.0%) \u2014 \u00b1$35/share impact around IV.\n2. Exit multiple (16-24x) \u2014 \u00b1$45/share impact around IV.\n3. Freight recovery duration (1 vs 3 years) \u2014 \u00b1$50/share impact.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive response: If JBHT raises intermodal rates (as BNSF\narbitration winner requires), competitors (XPO, Hub Group, Knight-Swift) gain\npricing umbrella \u2014 negative for JBHT's market share but positive for industry\nmargins. Rating: -1 (modest headwind to volume growth).\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity: Positive \u2014 strong stock price enables cheap equity\nbuybacks (shares -4.9% in 2025) and low-cost capital for fleet replacement.\nNegative \u2014 a sustained drawdown would spook shippers but JBHT has no debt\nrefinancing risk (low leverage). Net: mildly positive reflexivity.\nStep 3.5-3. Customer evolution: Mainstream/late-adopter shippers are now\nreturning to intermodal after the 2023-25 trough; road-to-rail conversion is\naccelerating due to capacity regulations. LTV/CAC not calculable [Unconfirmed].\nChurn risk: low for dedicated contracts.\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nPriors (Layer 1.5): P(EPS above prior peak in 3 years) \u2248 75%; P(40% drawdown\nwithin 3 years of a peak) \u2248 35%.\nUpdate from Q2 2026 evidence: intermodal volume +10%, rev/load +11%, spot above\ncontract \u2192 recovery likelihood raised to ~65%.\nPosterior scenario probabilities:\n\n| Scenario | Prob | 2027E EPS | Multiple | Fair Value 12mo | 12-mo Return |\n|----------|------|-----------|----------|-----------------|--------------|\n| Bear \u2014 cycle rolls over; capacity returns; rate cuts fail | 25% | $6.50 | 14.5x | $94 | -66% |\n| Base \u2014 recovery matures; 2028 peak near prior peak | 45% | $9.75 | 20.5x | $200 | -27% |\n| Bull \u2014 2+ yr capacity-driven upcycle; beats 2022 peak | 20% | $11.50 | 22.5x | $260 | -6% |\n| Very Bull \u2014 structural intermodal super-cycle | 10% | $13.00 | 24.5x | $320 | +16% |\n| TOTAL EV | 100% | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2248 $198 | \u2248 -28% |\n\nProbability-weighted expected price: 0.25\u00d794 + 0.45\u00d7200 + 0.20\u00d7260 + 0.10\u00d7320\n= 23.5 + 90 + 52 + 32 = $197.50.\n\nMargin of Safety at T0: MoS = (198 \u2212 275.45)/198 = **-39%** (NONE).\n50% CI: $140 \u2013 $240. 80% CI: $94 \u2013 $320.\n\nStep 4-5. Expected Price & MoS:\n- IV point: $200 (blended: 0.70\u00d7cycle-adjusted $200 + 0.30\u00d7DCF $125 \u2248 $178-200)\n- MoS at T0: NEGATIVE 37-39%. Verdict: NO BUY.\n\nSECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nMarket-implied horizon: The price of $275.45, at ~27.5x 2027E consensus EPS\n($10.01), implies the market is looking through to 2028-29 PEAK-cycle earnings\n($11-13) and capitalizing them at 22-24x today. Market horizon \u2248 2-3 years.\nMy horizon: 3-5 years. Spread = My Horizon (4y) \u2212 Market Horizon (2.5y) \u2248 1.5y.\nThis is NOT sufficient (>2y required) to establish positive horizon arbitrage.\nIn fact, the negative spread means I am buying a peak that is closer to the\nmarket's discount window than to mine. Negative arbitrage \u2014 do not force it.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nStep 5-1. Conviction Score (15 max)\n1. Business Quality: 4.5/5 (Fortress moat, 12% ROIC, 13x+ interest coverage)\n2. Valuation Attractiveness: 1/5 (MoS -39% at T0)\n3. Macro Alignment: 2/5 (mild headwind \u2014 hike risk, elevated 10Y)\n4. Thesis Clarity: 3/5 (KPI: intermodal volume/rev per load/operating ratio)\n5. Execution Traceability: 4/5 (insider 20.4%; capex guide; buyback track record)\nTOTAL: 14.5/15 \u2014 but this is conviction in the \"AVOID\" conclusion, not a buy.\nDecay adjustment (-1 after 6 months without confirmation) applies to any\nre-evaluation.\n\nStep 5-3. Sizing Guidelines\nFor a NEW long at current prices: 0% (no buy).\nFor existing holders: TRIM 25-50% at $275+ into strength. The dividend yield\n(0.68%) offers no support for holding a full position at a -39% MoS.\nRe-entry framework:\n- Starter position (5% of full) at $170-180 (MoS 10-15%) ONLY IF freight cycle\n  data remains positive.\n- Full position (8-10%) at $150-155 (MoS 22-25%).\n- Aggressive investors may short 2-3% (Kelly-based) but with tight stop above\n  $300; the risk of another re-rating is real.\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short interest: 4.29% float, 2.48 DTC, MoM change -11.8% [Actual \u2014 Aggregator]\n  \u2192 shorts are NOT crowded; no squeeze fuel.\n- Institutional ownership: 79.91%; insider 20.43% [Actual \u2014 Aggregator]\n  \u2192 high alignment, but also high indexing/passive flows that cannot be relied\n  on as an edge.\n- Put/Call skew: [Unconfirmed \u2014 options data not in the pack or retrieved].\n- Sentiment: Sell-side mean PT $305, median $317, high $370, low $182.\n  Consensus is 11-15% ABOVE the current price \u2014 the market already prices the\n  recovery. [Actual \u2014 Aggregator]\n- Contrarian signal: 52-week high $299.76 vs current $275.45; stock +92% off\n  low. Momentum strong, but sentiment is extended.\n- Crowding Risk Score: 9/15 (moderate-high crowding in the \"freight recovery\"\n  trade). Position size reduction -1pp if I were long.\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nJBHT is a high-beta (1.30) cyclical. It belongs in a portfolio as a tactical\n\"freight-recovery\" expression with a 12-24-month horizon, NOT as a core compounder.\nGiven my macro regime weights (35% recession vs 35% reflation), adding a new\ncyclical long at a -39% MoS would increase portfolio drawdown risk without\nadequate compensation.\nIf the book holds no freight exposure and the investor believes in the recovery,\nthe correct vehicle entry is a HEDGED starter (or the common stock only below\n$180). If the book already holds transports/industrials, adding JBHT at $275\nconcentrates the same cyclical factor at a late point in the re-rating.\n\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\nKelly fraction for the expected return of -28% (as computed in Section 4) is\nNEGATIVE. Kelly criterion: f* = (p\u00b7b \u2212 q)/b where the distribution has\nnegative expectancy. Therefore the mathematical optimal is 0% weight (or a\nsmall short for aggressive investors who can tolerate the right tail \u2014 I do NOT\nrecommend a short without options/timing edge).\nIf a forced long, the Kelly-implied size would be \u2264 -0.5% \u2192 clamp to 0%.\nDiscrepancy check: Layer 5 (0%) vs Layer 6.5 (0%) \u2014 no gap \u2192 no re-analysis.\n\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nCatalysts (next 12 months):\n1. Q3 2026 earnings (late Oct 2026): Intermodal volume/revenue per load uptrend;\n   Zacks has raised Q3 estimates +6.5% in 60 days [Estimate].\n2. Contract-rate catch-up to spot (2027 bids): management said \"pushing where we\n   can and where we need to\" [Actual \u2014 Q2 2026 call excerpt].\n3. Continued buyback: shares -4.9% FY2025; at ~35x earnings the buyback yield\n   still contributes ~2% annually [Arithmetic].\n4. 2027 net-capex guide (if <$800M) signals continued FCF growth.\n\nRisks:\n1. Macro: Fed HIKE (33% odds) \u2192 freight demand rolls over; EPS could fall to\n   $6.00-6.50 and the stock to $90-110 (my bear case).\n2. Capacity return: 2023-24 precedent shows the trucking supply response is fast.\n3. BNSF concentration: single rail partner; 2018-19 arbitration over $100M+ was\n   resolved at ~$44M [Actual \u2014 TalkBusiness Oct 2019]; any re-litigation of the\n   commercial agreement is a downside [Unconfirmed \u2014 no current dispute found].\n4. Fuel/diesel spike: stagflation regime (20% weight) squeezes margins if lags\n   persist.\n5. Multiple compression simply from \"aging\" of the recovery: the market pays 40x\n   during the inflection, then 18-20x at maturity. That transition alone costs\n   -50% from here even if EPS hits base case.\n\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\nCommon Bear Triggers shared with the rest of a portfolio:\n- Fed hike (33% implied) \u2192 hurts all high-multiple / long-duration assets; JBHT\n  beta 1.30 amplifies.\n- Dollar strength \u2192 hurts exporters and import-driven intermodal volumes; also\n  coincides with risk-off.\n- Freight cycle \u2192 independent of equity beta; correlates with ISM manufacturing.\nTail correlation: JBHT with the broader market in a 2022-style drawdown \u2248 0.8\n(high-beta cyclical). In 2020 COVID shock, transports fell 40%+ in 6 weeks.\nConditional VaR: In a 2008/2020-style stress, JBHT EPS could fall to $4.00-4.50,\nprice to $60-80 \u2014 an 70-80% drawdown from T0. In a mild 2023-24-style recession,\nprice to $130-160 (-40-50%). CVaR (5% tail) \u2248 -65%.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (for future re-entry or continued holding)\n\nThesis KPI thresholds (confirmed quarterly):\n1. Intermodal volume growth: \u00b1>8% YoY \u2192 positive; <3% \u2192 thesis break.\n2. Intermodal revenue per load: >+5% YoY \u2192 pricing power intact; <0% \u2192 margin\n   deterioration.\n3. Operating ratio (intermodal): <90% \u2192 positive; >93% \u2192 downgrade.\n4. Spot vs contract (DAT): spot > contract for 6+ months \u2192 cycle late; watch\n   for inversion.\n5. Net capex guide: if 2027 guide >$1.0B \u2192 management is chasing the cycle \u2014\n   negative signal.\n6. Shares outstanding: continued -4%+ buyback at <20x forward earnings confirms\n   management discipline; buybacks at 28x+ forward is value destruction.\nRe-evaluation triggers: any single miss of the above, a Fed HIKE, or a spot-rate\ninversion below contract by >5%.\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis (same data):\n1. $275.45 = 40.2x trailing earnings and ~27.5x 2027E consensus \u2014 a valuation\n   that has historically marked cyclical tops, not entry points.\n2. Dry-van spot rates above contract (June 2026) signal contract catch-up, after\n   which pricing power fades \u2014 the classic late-recovery signal.\n3. The 2021-22 base effect: EPS peaked at $9.22, and the stock at peak traded\n   15x peak EPS; today it trades nearly 30x PEAK-implied-2028 EPS. Multiple to\n   peak-earnings has never been this high.\n4. Freight capacity returns within 12-18 months of rate spikes; the 2023-24\n   freight recession proved the downside.\n5. A Fed HIKE (33% odds, 2-in-3 remaining) would kill the recovery narrative;\n   EPS at $6.50 = $94 fair value (14.5x).\n6. Single-point BNSF concentration: one rail partner; past arbitration over\n   $100M+ shows the relationship is not frictionless.\n7. Operating margin 7.2% (FY2025) vs 8.3% 12-yr median; even at 9.3% margin,\n   the market pays 24x \u2014 a \"best case\" already in the price.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat:\n- Long-side strength: 6/10 \u2014 real recovery evidence (Q2 beat: +40% NI, +10%\n  volume, record spot rates), structural intermodal share gains, fortress moat.\n- Short-side (avoid) strength: 7/10 \u2014 mathematical valuation gap, base rates,\n  and multiple-to-peak earnings at historical extremes.\nGap = 1 (< 2). DOWNGRADE conviction on an aggressive short. The conclusion\n\"AVOID / no buy at current\" remains robust, but I acknowledge that the freight\nrecovery may continue for 18-24 more months and that momentum can push the\nstock to $300+. For this reason, I do NOT recommend initiating a short; I\nrecommend 0% weight and disciplined re-entry at lower prices.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial Data:\nNo Hindenburg-style activist report was found. [Unconfirmed] The prior BNSF\narbitration (2018-19) was the most significant litigation; resolved at $44.2M\n[Actual \u2014 TalkBusiness]. No current SEC/regulatory action known.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed Arguments (and when they become valid):\n1. \"Freight recovery is just starting \u2014 buy early.\" Killed because the price\n   already embeds 3 years of recovery. VALID ONLY IF 2028 EPS > $13.\n2. \"The market pays a quality premium to JBHT (24-26x mid-cycle).\" Killed\n   because the premium applied to PEAK earnings \u2014 historically that combination\n   (peak earnings \u00d7 peak multiple) is a sell signal. VALID ONLY IF the freight\n   cycle has structurally lengthened (i.e., the 2020s capacity contraction is\n   permanent).\n3. \"DCF is too conservative; cyclicals need the normalized-earnings method.\"\n   Accepted \u2014 which is why I use Engine 2 as primary. But even the generous\n   normalized method gives $200, not $275. VALID ONLY IF you raise 2027-28\n   margin to 10%+ AND hold 24x \u2014 the \"very bull\" scenario.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\nA. Methodology Audit: PASS. Engine 2 (Cyclical) with Engine 1 cross-check;\n   cycle position established; no single-method dependence.\nB. Valuation Audit: PASS. Mid-cycle margin 8.8% vs 8.3% median; WACC 10.25%\n   explicitly derived; terminal growth 2.5% \u2264 nominal GDP; multiples sanity\n   checked against 2022 peak behavior.\nC. Bias Audit: PASS (with note). I am aware of anchoring on the 40x trailing\n   P/E; the cycle-adjusted method is explicitly designed to neutralize that\n   trap. The remaining bias risk is OVERTIMATION of the \"late cycle\" signal;\n   this is mitigated by the 45% base-case recovery weight, which still yields\n   a negative MoS.\nD. Consistency Audit: PASS. All projections use fiscal-year aligned inputs;\n   TTM (2026-06-30) used only for current estimates; no mixing of share counts\n   (93.9M current vs 97.7M FY2025 weighted).\nE. Narrative Audit: PASS. No \"core + optionality\" mixing; no platform premium\n   applied to a pure freight cyclical.\nF. Red Team Audit: PASS. Full adversarial section performed; logic-gap score\n   recorded and incorporated into conviction.\nG. Data Integrity Audit: PASS with flags. (1) Vendor debt $1.467B vs my filed\n   components $1.704B \u2014 I disclosed my debt pick (LT debt + current portion +\n   operating leases \u2212 cash) and noted the vendor discrepancy. (2) The BNSF\n   \">$100M 2026\" claim in the research brief was misdated (it was a 2018\n   dispute, resolved ~$44M in 2019); I verified and corrected it. (3) Segment\n   revenue XBRL dimensions are absent from the pack \u2014 no sum-of-the-parts\n   performed; [Unconfirmed] status carried. (4) Effective tax rate is my own\n   24% assumption, flagged as such.\n\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\nDate: 2026-08-24 | T0 Price: $275.45 | IV: $200 (cycle-adjusted base; DCF\ncross-check $104-142)\nMoS: -39% | Expected 12-mo return: \u2248 -28% (prob-weighted scenarios)\nKey assumptions logged:\n- 2027E op margin 8.8%, revenue $14.15B, tax 24%, WACC 10.25%, exit multiple 20.5x\n- Freight recovery holds through 2027 but does NOT structurally beat the 2022 peak\n  by more than 20%.\n- Terminal growth 2.5%.\nRed-team concern logged: if the freight market is in a multi-year structural\nupswing (regulatory capacity destruction + intermodal conversion), EPS could reach\n$13 by 2028, fair value $280-310 \u2014 my \"avoid\" call would be wrong by 10-15%.\nConfidence in the \"avoid\" call: 65%.\nKPI to falsify: Q3 2026 intermodal volume >+10% AND revenue/load >+8% AND\n2027 initial guidance suggesting EPS >$10.50 would raise bull-scenario weights\nto 40% and push IV to ~$235 \u2014 still a \"hold/small starter\" conclusion, not a buy.\n\nSECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\nACTION: DO NOT BUY / AVOID at $275.45. | Conviction: High (14.5/15 on\nframework, but in the \"avoid\" direction)\nPosition weight: 0% (NEW money). Existing holders: TRIM 25-50% into strength;\nmove to underweight vs benchmark.\nStrategy:\n1) Place no new capital at $275.45.\n2) Re-entry starter (4-5% position) at $170-180 IF the freight cycle data\n   remains positive (TTM consensus intact, spot > contract, volume >+8%).\n3) Full position (8-10%) at $150-165 (MoS 20-25%).\n4) Shorting is NOT recommended (right-tail risk too high; logic-gap score < 2).\n5) If already long and the price exceeds $300 while business data confirms,\n   continue trimming; do not add.\n6) Monitoring: quarterly data per Section 8; revisit in 90 days after Q3 2026\n   earnings (late Oct 2026).\nFinal one-line summation: JBHT is a fortress-quality cyclical at a price that\nhas already fully discounted a flawless recovery \u2014 pay $200, not $275.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nEND OF RS2 v2.0 ANALYSIS \u2014 JBHT 2026-08-24\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\