ggregator/Arithmetic] on a cyclical peak-recovery EPS.\n2. FY27 consensus EPS of $10.12 [Estimate, S&P Global] still only gives 27x earnings at $275.\n3. Adjusted FCF yield ~3.7% [Estimate] is below the 10-Yr Treasury yield.\n4. The freight recovery is real but late-stage; spot/contract spreads can roll over fast.\n5. DCS/ICS/FMS are low-margin and increasingly competitive; truckload is loss-making.\n6. Legacy BNSF/intermodal contract disputes introduce unquantified cash-flow risk.\n7. 79.9% institutional ownership [Aggregator] means index/ETF outflows will amplify downside.\n\nLong logic:\n1. Wide moat (13/21 moat score), 20.4% insider ownership [Aggregator].\n2. Volume records, Eastern network share gains, pricing recovery.\n3. Strong balance sheet; buybacks reducing share count every year.\n\nLogic combat score: Long 7/10, Short 7/10 \u2192 gap <2, conviction downgrade required. In this case, valuation asymmetry decides the call: at a +44% premium to expected value, the short logic prevails on a risk/reward basis.\n\nKilled arguments:\n- \u201cBNSF is about to owe JBHT $100M+\u201d: this is a legacy, already-disclosed dispute (WSJ 2018); no incremental material change is established.\n- \u201cMarket share >24%\u201d: the cited market-share figures are segment/methodology-dependent and unusable for valuation.\n- \u201cNew intermodal record means new profit plateau\u201d: records were set in volume, not in segment operating margin, which remains below prior peaks.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25